Two of these are worth reading closely. A1, A4 and A6 also kill the live case, because
on the real tree the budgets are behind both a continuation and a `&&`: break either
and `flags_by_gate()` loses them from the local side, which is precisely how a rule
like this becomes decorative without anything failing. B2 points CI at
`scripts/ci/ignored-tests-baseline.tsv`, a file that exists, so the dangling-call-site
rule cannot be what turns the checker red; the only thing that can is the disagreement
itself. A7 is the quietest mutation in the set -- the line still prints, the count does
not grow, and the exit status stays 0 -- and it is caught by the fixture that asserts
the exit status rather than the output.

