Both commands below run against the working tree this batch produces, and the second is
the whole self-test rather than the new class alone, because the reachability and mirror
rules read the same files the new reader reads.

$ python3 scripts/ci/check-guard-wiring.py
    check-guard-wiring: OK (50 files in scripts/ci/, 49 reachable, 45 run by scripts/verify-in-docker.sh, 4 recorded CI-only, 1 exempt)
    [exit 0]

$ python3 scripts/ci/test-check-guard-wiring.py
    ----------------------------------------------------------------------
    Ran 25 tests in 2.869s
    OK
